# Testing Guidelines

## 🧪 **Testing Strategy**

### **Test Pyramid:**
1. **Unit Tests** (70%) - Fast, isolated, test individual components
2. **Integration Tests** (20%) - Test component interactions
3. **End-to-End Tests** (10%) - Test complete user workflows

### **Test Project Structure:**
```
ApiTemplate.Application.Tests/          # Unit tests for Application layer
ApiTemplate.Domain.Tests/              # Unit tests for Domain layer  
ApiTemplate.Infrastructure.Tests/      # Unit tests for Infrastructure layer
ApiTemplate.Presentation.Web.Tests/    # Unit tests for Presentation layer
ApiTemplate.Presentation.Web.Tests.Integration/  # Integration tests
```

## 🔬 **Unit Testing Patterns**

### **Test Class Structure:**
```csharp
[TestFixture]
public class AccountServiceTests
{
    private Mock<IUserManager<Account>> _mockUserManager;
    private Mock<IMapper> _mockMapper;
    private AccountService _accountService;
    
    [SetUp]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _mockUserManager = new Mock<IUserManager<Account>>();
        _mockMapper = new Mock<IMapper>();
        _accountService = new AccountService(_mockUserManager.Object, _mockMapper.Object);
    }
    
    [Test]
    public async Task CreateAccount_ValidInput_ReturnsAccountDTO()
    {
        // Arrange
        var createDto = new CreateAccountDTO { Email = "test@example.com" };
        var account = new Account { Email = createDto.Email };
        var accountDto = new AccountDTO { Email = createDto.Email };
        
        _mockMapper.Setup(m => m.Map<Account>(createDto)).Returns(account);
        _mockUserManager.Setup(m => m.CreateAsync(account, createDto.Password))
                       .ReturnsAsync(IdentityResult.Success);
        _mockMapper.Setup(m => m.Map<AccountDTO>(account)).Returns(accountDto);
        
        // Act
        var result = await _accountService.CreateAccountAsync(createDto);
        
        // Assert
        Assert.That(result.Email, Is.EqualTo(createDto.Email));
        _mockUserManager.Verify(m => m.CreateAsync(account, createDto.Password), Times.Once);
    }
}
```

### **Naming Conventions:**
```csharp
// Test method naming: MethodName_Scenario_ExpectedResult
[Test]
public async Task CreateAccount_ValidInput_ReturnsAccountDTO()
[Test]
public async Task CreateAccount_InvalidEmail_ThrowsDomainException()
[Test]
public async Task GetAccount_NonExistentId_ReturnsNull()
```

### **AAA Pattern:**
- **Arrange**: Set up test data and mocks
- **Act**: Execute the method under test
- **Assert**: Verify the results

## 🔗 **Integration Testing**

### **Base Integration Test:**
```csharp
public abstract class BaseIntegrationTest
{
    protected WebApplicationFactory<Program> Factory { get; private set; }
    protected HttpClient Client { get; private set; }
    protected ApplicationDbContext Context { get; private set; }
    
    [OneTimeSetUp]
    public virtual async Task OneTimeSetUp()
    {
        Factory = new WebApplicationFactory<Program>()
            .WithWebHostBuilder(builder =>
            {
                builder.ConfigureServices(services =>
                {
                    // Remove real database
                    var descriptor = services.SingleOrDefault(d => d.ServiceType == typeof(DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext>));
                    if (descriptor != null) services.Remove(descriptor);
                    
                    // Add test database
                    services.AddDbContext<ApplicationDbContext>(options =>
                        options.UseInMemoryDatabase(databaseName: Guid.NewGuid().ToString()));
                    
                    ConfigureServices(services);
                });
            });
        
        Client = Factory.CreateClient();
        Context = Factory.Services.GetRequiredService<ApplicationDbContext>();
        await Context.Database.EnsureCreatedAsync();
    }
    
    protected virtual void ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection services)
    {
        // Override services for testing
    }
}
```

### **Integration Test Example:**
```csharp
[TestFixture]
public class AccountTests : BaseIntegrationTest
{
    [Test]
    public async Task CreateAccount_ValidInput_ReturnsCreatedAccount()
    {
        // Arrange
        var createDto = new CreateAccountDTO
        {
            Email = "test@example.com",
            Password = "TestPassword123!",
            FirstName = "Test",
            LastName = "User"
        };
        
        // Act
        var response = await Client.PostAsJsonAsync("/api/account", createDto);
        
        // Assert
        response.StatusCode.Should().Be(HttpStatusCode.Created);
        var account = await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<AccountDTO>();
        account.Email.Should().Be(createDto.Email);
        
        // Verify database
        var dbAccount = await Context.Accounts.FirstOrDefaultAsync(a => a.Email == createDto.Email);
        dbAccount.Should().NotBeNull();
    }
}
```

## 🎭 **Mocking Patterns**

### **Mock Setup:**
```csharp
// Setup return values
_mockUserManager.Setup(m => m.CreateAsync(It.IsAny<Account>(), It.IsAny<string>()))
               .ReturnsAsync(IdentityResult.Success);

// Setup with parameters
_mockUserManager.Setup(m => m.FindByEmailAsync("test@example.com"))
               .ReturnsAsync(new Account { Email = "test@example.com" });

// Setup exceptions
_mockUserManager.Setup(m => m.CreateAsync(It.IsAny<Account>(), It.IsAny<string>()))
               .ThrowsAsync(new DomainException("User already exists"));

// Verify calls
_mockUserManager.Verify(m => m.CreateAsync(It.IsAny<Account>(), It.IsAny<string>()), Times.Once);
_mockUserManager.Verify(m => m.AddToRoleAsync(It.IsAny<Account>(), "Admin"), Times.Never);
```

### **Mock Best Practices:**
- Use `It.IsAny<T>()` for flexible parameter matching
- Use `It.Is<T>(predicate)` for specific conditions
- Verify important interactions
- Don't over-mock (test real behavior when possible)

## 📊 **Test Data Management**

### **Test Data Builders:**
```csharp
public class AccountBuilder
{
    private Account _account = new Account();
    
    public AccountBuilder WithEmail(string email)
    {
        _account.Email = email;
        return this;
    }
    
    public AccountBuilder WithName(string firstName, string lastName)
    {
        _account.FirstName = firstName;
        _account.LastName = lastName;
        return this;
    }
    
    public AccountBuilder WithRole(RoleEnum role)
    {
        _account.Role = role;
        return this;
    }
    
    public Account Build() => _account;
}

// Usage
var account = new AccountBuilder()
    .WithEmail("test@example.com")
    .WithName("Test", "User")
    .WithRole(RoleEnum.Admin)
    .Build();
```

