```

### **Test Execution (Manual Only):**
```bash
# Run all tests (user must execute manually)
dotnet test

# Run specific category (user must execute manually)
dotnet test --filter Category=Unit

# Run with coverage (user must execute manually)
dotnet test --collect:"XPlat Code Coverage"

# Run specific project (user must execute manually)
dotnet test ApiTemplate.Application.Tests
```

**⚠️ IMPORTANT: Tests should only be run with explicit user command. Never run tests automatically.**

## 🎯 **Testing Best Practices**

### **DO:**
- Write tests that are fast, isolated, and repeatable
- Use descriptive test names that explain the scenario
- Test both success and failure cases
- Use meaningful assertions with clear error messages
- Keep tests simple and focused on one behavior

### **DON'T:**
- Test implementation details (test behavior instead)
- Create overly complex test setups
- Ignore failing tests
- Write tests that depend on external services
- Test framework code (test your code instead)